docs/workflows.md:770:`max_concurrency` controls how many independent parts run at the same time. Both `max_concurrency` and the compatibility key `max_parts` accept at most `3`; a larger value fails workflow loading. When neither is set, the default is `3`. When specified, `initial_max_parts` limits only the first decomposition batch. There is no total-part limit for the workflow step; the Team Leader adds batches until it decides no additional work is required or stops returning new unique parts. The scheduler requests a new batch only after every part in the current batch completes, so parts in one batch must never depend on each other; verification that needs implementation results belongs in a later batch. With `fail_on_part_error: true`, a generated-part failure can still lead the Team Leader to plan and run new recovery parts; it then ends the step with an error. When omitted, the leader can continue according to its normal recovery flow. The older `max_parts` key is still accepted as the compatibility name for `max_concurrency`. `refill_threshold` is a compatibility key and may only be omitted or set to `0`; non-zero values fail workflow loading because incremental refill conflicts with the batch barrier. `part_tags` sets provider routing tags on generated part steps. When omitted, parts inherit the parent step's `tags`. Empty and whitespace-only tags are invalid. `part_tags` is resolved through normal `provider_routing.tags`, so tag routing takes priority over persona routing from `part_persona`.
